<p class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</p>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: First-time Visitors Rainy Weather</h1>
<p>Somewhere in every first visit to Hanoi there is a day when the sky changes the plan, and for a first-time visitor on a 50cc that day is a test of preparation rather than courage. Rain in this city tends to arrive hard and leave, it turns paint, metal covers, and tram rails into ice, and it turns a confident new rider into a careful one, which is exactly what the situation wants. The verified rate for a 50cc scooter is 200,000 VND per day, the shop sits at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, and a wet day on the rental is still a day well spent if it is planned as a wet day.</p>
<p>It belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental hub for Hanoi</a> and follows our <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/first-time-visitors-route-suitability/">route suitability guide for first-time visitors</a>, because the rain's biggest effect is on the map. For what a rental costs in any weather, the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost overview</a> lists every verified price, and the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> answers the counter questions we hear on bright mornings and grey ones alike. This page is for the grey ones.</p>
